            <ArticleTitle>Existential pain: impressions from an American Indian reservation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The existential suffering of members of the Havasupai Indian tribe are described by a physician-anthropologist who spent some time serving as an interim medical provider for the tribe. Pain is often described as having both physical and emotional dimensions. In this paper, the existential dimension is explored through a narrative of the author's experiences.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
